{{DISPLAYTITLE: <span style="color: #b300b3;">Wall Breakers</span>}}
{{Protection}}{{MagicWords}}{{ClashofClansLink|Wall Breaker}}

{{Card Infobox|Cost=2|Rarity=Epic|Type=Troop|Arena=Spooky Town|ReleaseDate=26 February 2019}}{{SubpageNavBox|Evolution=yes}}{{Quote|A daring duo of dangerous dive bombers. Nothing warms a Wall Breaker's cold and undead heart like blowing up buildings.}}

The Wall Breakers is an {{Rarity|Epic}} [[Cards|card]] that is unlocked from the [[Arenas|Spooky Town (Arena 12)]]. It spawns two very fast, area-damage, building-targeting, melee, ground [[:Category:Troop Cards|troop]] with low hitpoints and very high damage. They drop their barrel at their target when attacking, destroying themselves in the process on impact. Their deployment is in a horizontal formation. They resemble [[Skeletons]] donning team-colored bandannas and carry explosive barrels. A Wall Breakers card costs 2 [[Elixir]] to deploy.

==Strategy==
{{Battle Deck with Card|:Category:Battle Decks using the Wall Breakers Card}}
*For just 2 [[Elixir]], Wall Breakers can force an enemy response, as they threaten to take out around 20% of a [[:Category:Tower Troop Cards|Crown Tower]]'s health if ignored.
*It also can be a huge threat if the opposing player has Wall Breakers along with [[Clone]] and [[Mirror]], releasing 8 Wall Breakers being able to instantly destroy a +1 leveled Crown Tower for 8 Elixir. Consider baiting spells like [[The Log]], [[Barbarian Barrel]], [[Arrows]], and 360° attackers like [[Valkyrie]], [[Dark Prince]], and [[Mega Knight]].
*Wall Breakers are especially effective in [[Battle Decks|decks]] with several low-cost [[cards]], as their own low cost combined with other low-cost cards can cause the opponent's best counter to them to not be available when the player deploys them multiple times in a row, forcing them to defend inefficiently.
*Due to the Wall Breakers being in pairs, the player can split them into separate lanes by deploying them in the middle of the [[Arenas|Arena]]. This is an effective way to divide their attacks, as countering this attack Elixir-efficiently is somewhat difficult.
*The Wall Breakers do area damage. [[Tornado]] can be used to group up enemy troops just as they explode for a potentially high Elixir profit.
*Staggering the Wall Breakers 1 tile to either side of the bridge instead of placing them directly in front will allow the Wall Breakers to connect slightly sooner to a Crown Tower, since the outer Wall Breaker will push the inner Wall Breaker slightly forward as they run onto the enemy's side.
*Wall Breakers have shockingly high defensive use despite their low hitpoints and lack of damage. Its high movement speed is especially helpful when kiting troops with Fast or Very Fast movement speed. This helps stall melee troops with similar movement speeds, like the Lumberjack. To do this, place them two tiles into the opposite lane and three tiles from the bridge. If timed properly, the attacker will be slightly chipped by Crown Towers and chase the Wall Breakers ineffectively, allowing them to connect unless more Elixir is committed. Either outcome benefits the defender; valuable damage for 2 Elixir or a positive Elixir trade. This tactic also works against the [[Bandit]]; her dash often misses due to their speed, though she still needs to be defended afterward. A variant of this is to wait for the troop to be halfway between the bridge and Tower Troop, then place the Wall Breakers at the bridge.
*[[Arrows]] and [[Royal Delivery]] will completely destroy the Wall Breakers, but for a negative Elixir trade. This is not necessarily a bad decision, as letting them connect freely more than once is usually detrimental. In the case of the Royal Delivery, a [[Royal Recruits|Royal Recruit]] will also spawn to assist in defense.
*[[The Log]], [[Zap]], [[Barbarian Barrel]], and [[Giant Snowball]] will all deal enough damage to the Wall Breakers that the Crown Tower will be able to destroy them before they connect. This is an effective counter as long as they are not supported with a tank. If they are supported with a tank, an [[Ice Spirit]] can complement the defense well as it will be able to finish both of them off if played second, or will stall them and give the defender more time to counter them if played first.
*A lone Ice Spirit is one of the few cards which cannot fully defend Wall Breakers with the help of the Crown Tower. One will still be able to connect for notable chip damage, but it may be a worthwhile play if the player can make the most out of the 1 Elixir gained from the trade.
*When making a push with another troop who only targets buildings, Wall Breakers placed in the opposite lane can cripple or even destroy any defensive [[:Category:Building Cards|buildings]] placed in order to block it.
*If the player has already taken a Crown Tower, they can place the Wall Breakers in the middle of the opponent's side, giving their opponent very little time to react. However, only 1 Wall Breaker will connect, so quickly placing a tank beforehand will make this more effective.
*Using Wall Breakers with a small and cheap card such as Ice Spirit allows the player to cheaply tank for their Wall Breakers without spending much Elixir, and the Ice Spirit can freeze any troops the opponent might try to use to defeat the Wall Breakers.
*Combining the Wall Breakers with [[Rage]] makes them difficult to react to at the bridge and can result in both connecting to the tower if the opponent lacks area damage counters or buildings, but their damage won't be boosted, as Rage only increases attack speed and the Wall Breakers' damage is instant.
*Pairing the Wall Breakers with the [[Miner]] results in a cheap and efficiently threatening push since the Crown Tower will target the Miner first and allow the Wall Breakers to hit their mark. Even if the Wall Breakers are stopped, the Miner will have dealt chip damage, and often times eliminating both requires the same amount of Elixir.
*Wall Breakers do enough damage to destroy a [[Goblin Cage]] and release the Goblin Brawler.
*Using Zap along with a Wall Breakers push is especially effective against swarms, as the spell will not only get splash damage value but also supports the Wall Breakers with its 0.5 second stun and instantaneous deploy, possibly allowing them to connect with just a sliver of health.
*Wall Breakers from Level 6 to Level 8 will be destroyed in 3 hits by an equally levelled Crown Tower, but otherwise they take 4 hits. Additionally, if they are at least 1 level lower, the Crown Tower will always destroy a Wall Breaker in 3 hits. Since a Wall Breaker being destroyed in 3 hits means that one will fail to connect, the player should keep this in mind when deciding to use them.
*Paired with a [[Giant]] or [[Golem]], the Wall Breakers can rush to the Crown Tower as either tank will tank the damage from Crown Tower.
*The Wall Breakers should never be used in conjunction with the [[Rune Giant]]. The Rune Giant will enhance their damage, but it will never activate due to them destroying themselves with their first attack, effectively wasting her ability.
*An activated [[King's Tower]] is an enormous problem for a Wall Breakers user. The King Tower will be able to hit and kill one Wall Breaker with the assistance of their Crown Tower, which would result in only the second Wall Breaker connecting. Try not to have troops in your deck that are exploitable for King Tower activations like [[Electro Spirit]], [[Magic Archer]], [[Bomber/Evolution|Evolved Bomber]], and [[Firecracker]].

