==History==
2019
*The Wall Breakers were once available in the [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|Wall Breakers Draft Challenge]] which started on 14/2/2019. In this [[Tournament|challenge]], gameplay was similar to a regular Draft Challenge, except that one of the players was able to choose who would use the Wall Breakers. If the player achieved at least 8 wins, they obtained the Wall Breakers early.
*From 20/2/2019 through 22/2/2019, the [[Shop]] had a special offer where [[Arenas|Arena]] 1+ players could buy up to 4 special Fortune [[Chests]] for 500 [[Gems]] that guarantee at least 50% of the Chest's contents to be Wall Breakers. The Chest was able to generate up to 150% of its contents to be Wall Breakers.
*The Wall Breakers [[Cards|card]] was generally released on 26/2/2019.
*On 4/3/2019, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (4/3/2019)|Balance Update]], decreased the Wall Breakers' attack time to 1.2 seconds (from 1.5 seconds).
*On 6/5/2019, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (6/5/2019)|Balance Update]], increased the Wall Breakers' damage by 10%, their range to 0.5 tiles (from 0.25 tiles), and re-centered their splash radius to damage nearby troops when attacking. The damage increase was not stated in the balance update video but is mentioned in the [https://clashroyale.com/blog/release-notes/balance-update-coming-5-6.html official release notes] and on the [https://twitter.com/ClashRoyale/status/1125306820904595456 Clash Royale Twitter page].
*On 3/6/2019, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (3/6/2019)|Balance Update]], changed the sound and visual effects of the Wall Breakers.
*On 7/10/2019, a [[Version History#Pass Royale and more (7/10/2019)|Balance Update]], decreased the Wall Breaker's cost to 2 [[Elixir]] (from 3 Elixir), decreased their damage by 10%, increased their mass to 4 (from 2), and decreased their collision radius to 0.4 tiles (from 0.5 tiles). The deploy position of the Wall Breakers was also tweaked slightly, putting them a bit closer together.
*On 4/11/2019, a [[Version History#Pass Royale and more (4/11/2019)|Balance Update]], decreased the Wall Breakers' damage by 19% and decreased their area radius to 1.5 tiles (from 2 tiles). They also now spawn further apart.
*On 26/11/2019, the [[Version History#End%20of%20November%202019%20Update%20(26/11/2019)|End of November 2019 Update]], added a card render to the Wall Breakers' card info screen.
2020
*On 2/6/2020, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (2/6/2020)|Balance Update]], gave the Wall Breakers a new 0.1 seconds deploy stagger from each other.
2021
*On 7/6/2021, the [[Version History#Summer%202021%20Update%20(7/6/2021)|Summer 2021 Update]], moved the Arena to unlock the Wall Breakers from Training Camp to Spell Valley.
*On 27/10/2021, the [[Version History#Champions%20Update%20(27/10/2021)|Champions Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 14 (from 13).
2022
*On 27/6/2022, the [[Version History#Summer%202022%20Update%20(27/6/2022)|Summer 2022 Update]], added the No Escape [[Card Mastery]] task for the Wall Breakers.
*On 26/10/2022, the [[Version History#2022%20Quarter%203%20Update%20(26/10/2022)|2022 Quarter 3 Update]], moved the Arena to unlock the Wall Breakers from Spell Valley to Spooky Town.
2023
*On 19/6/2023, the [[Version History#Card%20Evolution%20Update%20(19/6/2023)|Card Evolution Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 15 (from 14).
2024
*On 14/2/2024, the Wall Breakers' Evolution was added.
2025
*On 31/3/2025, the [[Version History#2025 Quarter 1 Update (31/3/2025)|2025 Quarter 1 Update]], decreased the Wall Breakers' hitpoints by 0.3%, and their damage by 0.25%.
*On 3/11/2025, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (2/6/2020)|Balance Update]], decreased the Wall Breakers’ damage by 10%. 
2026

* On 4/8/2026, a Balance Update, decreased the Wall Breakers’ damage by 20%

